Upstream source code
--------------------
TimelineXray does not include or redistribute source code from the xai-org/x-algorithm
repository: it is not vendored. That code is fetched at runtime from the public repository
into a local snapshot store and remains under its own license and notices. At commit
77d431aabf409ca1c1eed9bec7e2183f7c914e23 its root LICENSE file is the Apache License 2.0,
and it contains component-level NOTICE files (for example one for MIT-licensed code in
abuse-ledger-service) that TimelineXray's license inventory lists for every pinned commit.
Keep those notices with any upstream material you redistribute.

The goldens (goldens/citations.json) and the documentation cite upstream code by commit,
path, line numbers, SHA-256 and short anchor strings (at most 80 characters); they contain
no upstream source files.

Names and marks
---------------
"X" and "xAI" are used only to identify the public repository this tool analyses. This
project uses no X or xAI logos or other brand assets and claims no affiliation.

Third-party software
--------------------
TimelineXray has no third-party runtime dependencies. It uses the Python standard library
and runs the system git executable as a separate program; neither is bundled. Building a
distribution uses setuptools (MIT License), which is not included in the built packages.
